  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0025\" consists of five tables: `silk_profile`, `silk_profile_queries`, `silk_request`, `silk_response`, and `silk_sqlquery`.\nThe `silk_profile` table is used to store information about the performance profiles of the application. It includes columns such as `id`, `name`, `start_time`, `end_time`, `time_taken`, `file_path`, `line_num`, `end_line_num`, `func_name`, `exception_raised`, `dynamic`, and `request_id`. The `request_id` column is a foreign key referencing the `id` column in the `silk_request` table.\nThe `silk_profile_queries` table stores information about which queries were part of a particular profile. It includes columns such as `id`, `profile_id`, and `sqlquery_id`. The `sqlquery_id` and `profile_id` columns are foreign keys referencing the `id` column in the `silk_sqlquery` and `silk_profile` tables respectively.\nThe `silk_request` table stores information about the requests made to the application. It includes columns such as `id`, `path`, `query_params`, `raw_body`, `body`, `method`, `start_time`, `view_name`, `end_time`, `time_taken`, `encoded_headers`, `meta_time`, `meta_num_queries`, `meta_time_spent_queries`, `pyprofile`, `num_sql_queries`, and `prof_file`.\nThe `silk_response` table stores information about the responses returned by the application. It includes columns such as `id`, `status_code`, `raw_body`, `body`, `encoded_headers`, and `request_id`. The `request_id` column is a foreign key referencing the `id` column in the `silk_request` table.\nFinally, the `silk_sqlquery` table stores information about the SQL queries made by the application. It includes columns such as `id`, `query`, `start_time`, `end_time`, `time_taken`, `traceback`, `request_id`, and `identifier`. The `request_id` column is a foreign key referencing the `id` column in the `silk_request` table. The `silk_profile`, `silk_profile_queries`, `silk_request`, `silk_response`, and `silk_sqlquery` tables are interconnected, with foreign keys ensuring referential integrity and maintaining the integrity of the data.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context:\n\nSilk is a live profiling and inspection tool specifically designed for the Django framework. It serves as a performance analysis system by intercepting and storing HTTP requests and database queries. This allows developers to inspect and visualize runtime operations through a user interface, facilitating debugging and optimization.\n\nObjectives:\n\nThe primary objective of Silk is to provide real-time insights into the performance of Django applications. This includes profiling HTTP requests, responses, SQL queries, and code blocks, helping developers identify and resolve bottlenecks.\n\nStakeholders & Users:\n\n- Primary Users: Django developers needing real-time profiling and diagnostics.\n- Stakeholders: Development teams, Quality Assurance teams, Project Managers, and any entity involved in Django application performance optimization.\n\nFunctional Descriptions:\n\n1. Middleware Integration: Integrates as middleware to intercept and log HTTP requests and responses for profiling purposes.\n   \n2. SQL Query Profiling: Wraps around SQL execution to capture and profile database queries, allowing analysis of query performance.\n\n3. Code Profiling: Utilizes a context manager and decorator to enable profiling of specific code blocks or functions, giving developers flexibility in what to profile.\n\n4. User Interface: Provides a graphical user interface for inspecting and visualizing the captured data, including HTTP transactions and SQL queries.\n\n5. Data Relationships: Maintains data relationships, such as linking requests to their corresponding SQL queries, to provide comprehensive profiling context.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions:\n\n- Performance: The system should minimally impact the performance of the application being profiled to ensure accurate representations of typical operation scenarios.\n\n- Usability: The user interface should be intuitive, enabling quick access and understanding of the profiling data without requiring extensive training.\n\n- Scalability: Must efficiently handle large volumes of requests and queries, ensuring it remains effective in high-traffic environments.\n\n- Security: Ensures that sensitive data captured during profiling is securely handled, adhering to data protection standards.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0025.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0025\nCREATE TABLE `silk_profile` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `time_taken` float NOT NULL,\n  `file_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `line_num` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `end_line_num` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `func_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `exception_raised` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `dynamic` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `request_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `silk_profile_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`request_id`) REFERENCES `silk_request` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `silk_profile_queries` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `profile_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sqlquery_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `silk_profile_queries_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`profile_id`) REFERENCES `silk_profile` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `silk_profile_queries_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`sqlquery_id`) REFERENCES `silk_sqlquery` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `silk_request` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `query_params` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `raw_body` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `body` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `method` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `view_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `time_taken` float NOT NULL,\n  `encoded_headers` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `meta_time` float NOT NULL,\n  `meta_num_queries` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `meta_time_spent_queries` float NOT NULL,\n  `pyprofile` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `num_sql_queries` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `prof_file` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `silk_response` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `status_code` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `raw_body` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `body` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `encoded_headers` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `silk_response_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`request_id`) REFERENCES `silk_request` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `silk_sqlquery` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `query` text NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `time_taken` float NOT NULL,\n  `traceback` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `identifier` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `silk_sqlquery_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`request_id`) REFERENCES `silk_request` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
